{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Time-independent perturbation theory and the anharmonic oscillator",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "K. Dirac — Advanced Quantum Mechanics, Lecture 7",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Setting up the problem",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We seek eigenstates of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "H = H_0 + \\lambda V",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " where the spectrum of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "H_0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is known, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "H_0|n^{(0)}\\rangle = E_n^{(0)}|n^{(0)}\\rangle",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is small. Expanding",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_n = E_n^{(0)} + \\lambda E_n^{(1)} + \\lambda^2 E_n^{(2)} + \\cdots,\\qquad |n\\rangle = |n^{(0)}\\rangle + \\lambda|n^{(1)}\\rangle + \\cdots",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:expand",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "and collecting powers of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_n^{(1)} = \\langle n^{(0)}|V|n^{(0)}\\rangle,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:e1",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_n^{(2)} = \\sum_{m\\neq n}\\frac{|\\langle m^{(0)}|V|n^{(0)}\\rangle|^2}{E_n^{(0)}-E_m^{(0)}}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:e2",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Note that ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:e2",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " is always negative for the ground state: second-order corrections push the lowest level down.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The quartic oscillator",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Take ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "H_0 = \\hbar\\omega(a^\\dagger a + \\tfrac12)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "V = x^4",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "x = \\sqrt{\\hbar/2m\\omega}\\,(a + a^\\dagger)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Using ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "a|n\\rangle = \\sqrt n|n-1\\rangle",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " one finds",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\langle n|(a+a^\\dagger)^4|n\\rangle = 6n^2 + 6n + 3,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:x4",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "so the first-order shift is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_n^{(1)} = \\frac{3\\hbar^2}{4m^2\\omega^2}\\left(2n^2 + 2n + 1\\right).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:shift",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The non-zero off-diagonal elements connect ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " to ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n\\pm2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n\\pm4",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". For the ground state the second-order result is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_0 = \\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2} + \\frac{3\\lambda\\hbar^2}{4m^2\\omega^2} - \\frac{21\\lambda^2\\hbar^3}{8m^4\\omega^5} + \\mathcal O(\\lambda^3).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:e0",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Degenerate case",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "If ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E^{(0)}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "g",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "-fold degenerate, diagonalise ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "V",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " within the degenerate subspace:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\det\\left[\\langle n_i^{(0)}|V|n_j^{(0)}\\rangle - E^{(1)}\\delta_{ij}\\right] = 0.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:secular",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The linear Stark effect in hydrogen ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n = 2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the classic example: the field mixes ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "2s",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "2p_0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", splitting them by ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\pm 3 e a_0 \\mathcal E",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Validity",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The series is asymptotic, not convergent — Dyson's argument ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "dyson1952"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " shows that for ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda < 0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the potential is unbounded below, so ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E(\\lambda)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " cannot be analytic at ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda = 0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Optimal truncation is at the smallest term.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Problems",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Compute the first-order shift for V = x³. Why does it vanish?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Derive the second-order shift for V = x³ and compare with the exact result for V = κx.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Apply degenerate perturbation theory to a 2D isotropic oscillator perturbed by λxy.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{thebibliography}{99}\n\\bibitem{dyson1952} F. J. Dyson, \\emph{Phys. Rev.} \\textbf{85}, 631 (1952).\n\\end{thebibliography}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    }
  ],
